{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451108-can-a-clan-adopt-a-caitiff","id":1451108,"title":"Can a Clan Adopt a Caitiff?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-05T22:19:21-07:00","id":1451108,"title":"Can a Clan Adopt a Caitiff?","content":"So. I\u2019m working on an idea, for a Caitiff. But the general idea, is that he was the abandoned Childer of a City Gangrel Sabbat, whose Clan Curse, basically went to town on him, when he was embraced, rather than just being a Caitiff. Leaving him hideous, and looking more like a Were-Bat.<br /> <br /> In the end, the idea, is that he was found by Nosferatu, and more or less taken in by them, and permitted to sleep outside the Warrens in the Sewer, and serve as a Guard-Dog of sorts. He does have the Clan Friendship merit with them after-all.<br /> <br /> So, I suppose my question is. Could a Clan adopt a Caitiff? Unofficially? In the sense that, if anyone asked they would bullshit, and be like, \u201cHe\u2019s a Nosferatu, fuck off, Blueblood.\u201d<br /> <br /> Would the nature of being rendered Monstrous, with an Appearance of 0, and looking like more of a Beast than man, have made them more or less likely to take him in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12039-punkmaniak","name":"PunkManiak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12039_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T22:20:35-07:00","id":1451109,"title":"","content":"This is basically what he looks like. He\u2019s an Amnesiac, without any memory of his life Pre-Embrace.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://i.postimg.cc/NMCQvLRy/4077-EAB2-280-E-4315-894-F-B199-C3783-EDF.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.postimg.cc/NMCQvLRy/4077-EAB2-280-E-4315-894-F-B199-C3783-EDF.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.postimg.cc/NMCQvLRy/4077-EAB2-280-E-4315-894-F-B199-C3783-EDF.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://i.postimg.cc/NMCQvLRy/4077-EAB2-280-E-4315-894-F-B199-C3783-EDF.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12039-punkmaniak","name":"PunkManiak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12039_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T22:30:57-07:00","id":1451111,"title":"","content":"Officially?<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> Unofficially, the OUTCASTS book says the Giovanni and other clans sometimes adopt Caitiff by passing them off as wayward childer. Its a central plot in WINTER'S TEETH in fact. You can also pass yourself off as a Brujah or Toreador with little difficulty and other Clans with more difficulty.<br /> <br /> Amusingly, the Followers of Set do this all the time and many Followers of Set are actually members of other Clans. Even orthodox typhonists are BARELY inclined to view converts as less than pure blooded members (because Set is the first vampire to them, this makes sense). The other Clans are AGHAST!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-06-2021, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T22:34:33-07:00","id":1451113,"title":"","content":"Surprised about the Toreador thing. The Torries have been a High Clan for a very long time. One would think they would know lineages almost as well as the Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T22:45:45-07:00","id":1451114,"title":"","content":"Of course a Clan could adopt a Caitiff. Well, not the entire Clan, but the local Clan members could. It wouldn\u2019t change the biology of the caitiff, but they could be accepted as a member of that Clan for all political purposes and treated as a member of that Clan. Potentially the secret could come out, but it probably wouldn\u2019t unless members of the adopting Clan decided to out the Caitiff for some reason. <br /> <br /> So they can do this, but would they? Maybe, it depends on the individuals in charge, but it\u2019s not unthinkable, especially for a Clan like the Nosferatu who aren\u2019t going to care much about pure heritage and may be favorably inclined towards outcasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T22:50:29-07:00","id":1451116,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> To be a little more clear. The character is an Amnesiac in a V20 game, with the Amnesia, Imperfect Understanding, and Monstrous Flaws.<br /> <br /> They do not know their clan, and unless a Tremere decides to test it, their clan and generation, are wholly unknown.<br /> <br /> As far as the character is aware, they woke up, in a pool of blood, and then the pain began, as their bones began to snap and twist, changing them into their new shape, leaving them screaming in Agony. I\u2019m thinking a Nosferatu took them in, to protect the Masquerade, and possibly taking pity on the young thing.<br /> <br /> In reality.....they were forcibly drained of blood, and then Embraced by a 7th Generation Sabbat City Gangrel, who wanted a new servant, upon awakening out of Torpor. When their blood caused their Childer to be twisted, misshapen, and completely inhuman in Appearance, they abandoned the project, because a Childer that could not blend in with Mortals, was worthless to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12039-punkmaniak","name":"PunkManiak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12039_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T22:53:24-07:00","id":1451118,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> Well. The image I linked in the second post, is what they look like. Aside from the more animalistic aspect of their appearance, and bat-like features, they can basically blend in perfectly with the Nosferatu, being equally hideous and unnerving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12039-punkmaniak","name":"PunkManiak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12039_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T23:29:08-07:00","id":1451119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451108-can-a-clan-adopt-a-caitiff?p=1451113#post1451113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surprised about the Toreador thing. The Torries have been a High Clan for a very long time. One would think they would know lineages almost as well as the Ventrue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Toreador have a history of also making sudden Embraces motivated by their Clan Flaw. They thus have a hefty number of poor choice Embraces. You probably could never get into the interior halls of perfectness unless you had a superior talent or wit at putting others down but being acknowledged as part of the CLAN is not that hard.<br /> <br /> Leopold the Sculptor for example (who was actually Tremere Antitribu).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T02:02:25-07:00","id":1451122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451108-can-a-clan-adopt-a-caitiff?p=1451111#post1451111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Officially?<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> Unofficially, the OUTCASTS book says the Giovanni and other clans sometimes adopt Caitiff by passing them off as wayward childer. Its a central plot in WINTER'S TEETH in fact. You can also pass yourself off as a Brujah or Toreador with little difficulty and other Clans with more difficulty.<br /> <br /> Amusingly, the Followers of Set do this all the time and many Followers of Set are actually members of other Clans. Even orthodox typhonists are BARELY inclined to view converts as less than pure blooded members (because Set is the first vampire to them, this makes sense). The other Clans are AGHAST!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, its seems the Puttanesca branch of the Giovanni specifically will let you work your way to an adoption. I've thought that interesting for a number of reasons.<br /> <br /> Setites and Baali will accept believers and have rituals for it. In the 1st ed Clanbook it was mentioned that Brujah would occasionally adopt standup Caitiff on the assumption that most Caitiff were from Brujah anyway. Not sure how the old Hellenes of the clan felt about it, but they can't go around being upset about everything the Iconoclasts do that they disagree with, they'd never get anything done.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T05:44:57-07:00","id":1451128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451108-can-a-clan-adopt-a-caitiff?p=1451111#post1451111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amusingly, the Followers of Set do this all the time and many Followers of Set are actually members of other Clans. Even orthodox typhonists are BARELY inclined to view converts as less than pure blooded members (because Set is the first vampire to them, this makes sense). The other Clans are AGHAST!</div> </div> </div> </div>Would the Followers of Set (or the Baali) adopt a lost and largely clueless Caitiff? They are a Cult with a strong recruitment drive, but does that mean that they take in anyone? The Followers of Set have a lot to offer to a hypothetical Caitiff, but what can a young one offer to the Cult? I imagine a Caitiff who is somewhat established, skilled, and experienced would be welcomed.<br /> A young Vampire with no place for himself can be relatively easy to indoctrinate, so that is at least one reason the Setites might recruit one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-06-2021, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T07:12:14-07:00","id":1451132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451108-can-a-clan-adopt-a-caitiff?p=1451113#post1451113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surprised about the Toreador thing. The Torries have been a High Clan for a very long time. One would think they would know lineages almost as well as the Ventrue.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of Phaedymite Ravnos used to pass themselves off as Toreador, even up until the modern nights. This was frequently done in collusion with various Toreador as opposed to some sort of elaborate ruse. Generally speaking, high society has usually worked on the idea that if someone of reputation vouches for you, you're in. Though how long you actually stay &quot;in&quot; depends on how well you play the game. Or at least how long people find you interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T07:25:55-07:00","id":1451135,"title":"","content":"8th gen caitiff? Lol nope, your just a confused gangrel that frenzied way too often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T07:28:06-07:00","id":1451136,"title":"","content":"Probably not really relevant to most people here, but i think there was a VtES card that adressed the subject of Caitiffs being recognized as part of a certain lineage and joining (getting +1 blood potency bump in the process). Bringing it up because i like to mess around with those little divergences of the cardgame to VtM's lore.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now speaking of the character's specific background, i see no problem with it, unofficial adoption of individual kindred is a thing that can happen, specially if one possesses weaknesses or flaws that might make the ruse more convincing.<br /> <br /> And i'd say it's far from a Caitiff-only thing, as i can see a bunch of Cappadocian infitiores with conditions similar to <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Troglodytia\" target=\"_blank\">Troglodytia</a> joining the Nos, surviving the Giovanni Purge and maybe even making warrens of their own. Not to mention the occasional subtle Malk that ends up as Toreador, Tremere or Tzimisce and through twists of fate becomes the founder of some &quot;eccentric branch of the clan&quot; (Dracul/&quot;Old Clan&quot; Tzimisce?) centuries later, for another example of &quot;clan-jumping&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-10-2021, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T12:51:44-07:00","id":1451159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451108-can-a-clan-adopt-a-caitiff?p=1451128#post1451128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the Followers of Set (or the Baali) adopt a lost and largely clueless Caitiff? They are a Cult with a strong recruitment drive, but does that mean that they take in anyone? The Followers of Set have a lot to offer to a hypothetical Caitiff, but what can a young one offer to the Cult? I imagine a Caitiff who is somewhat established, skilled, and experienced would be welcomed.<br /> A young Vampire with no place for himself can be relatively easy to indoctrinate, so that is at least one reason the Setites might recruit one.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Followers of Set's case, a Caitiff is building material. Which is different from the way most Clans will be. One useless Caitiff today could be a fanatical devotee of Set later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T11:24:20-07:00","id":1451361,"title":"","content":"There are too many variables to really give concrete, universal answers on this one.<br /> <br /> Are we talking about a vampire who, due to one circumstance or another, didn't undergo the Becoming but which can prove lineage in some way?<br /> <br /> Are we talking about clans which hold lineage in equal or higher regard than generation itself? And of those, the clans that hold particular contempt for Caitiff for one reason or another, or might have taboos against the circumstances in which a vampire may fail the Becoming? Or, as mentioned earlier, don't particularly care for bloodline and hold social ties or allegiances in higher regard?<br /> <br /> I mean, let's look at one potential, extreme, example: a Caitiff sired by a Ventrue, who didn't undergo the Becoming for whatever reason but <i>can</i> prove their lineage. That's probably the worst-possible scenario for a Caitiff as their mere existence is a stain against the clan's sterling reputation, not to mention a condemning mark against their sire's dignitas provided that sire still has their unlife, but the bigger blow to dignitas is to <i>deny</i> that Caitiff's lineage by pure fiat. If for no other reason than to save face, the Gerousia would at least be bound to <i>hear</i> the Caitiff's case, even if it's a kangaroo court and the Gerousia can and would do anything in their power to find an excuse for disowning the Caitiff.<br /> <br /> Of course I'm also discussing a clan that could simply blood bond and dominate their way around this socially-sticky situation in any number of ways, largely depending upon the fledgling's potential usefulness and how strongly they conform to Ventrue norms. To the point a wayward fledgling with an inconvenient lineage, or circumstances behind their embrace, could simply be dominated to <i>believe</i> they have preferential taste in blood, can't learn out of clan disciplines, and that their sire is in fact someone entirely different...and anyone with evidence to the contrary made to believe otherwise or simply disappear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}